.TH RISKBASE 1 "August 2026" "RiskBase 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
riskbase \- internal CLI for regional threat posture assessments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B riskbase
[\-LR] [\-NRT] [\-\-json] [\-\-explain-score] [\-O path]
[\-\-residence-country value]
[\-\-clearance-level value]
[\-\-agency value]
[\-\-destination-country value]
[\-\-destination-city value]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B riskbase
produces a fast advisory posture and optional detailed evidence-backed report for travel movement decisions.
It is intended for internal operational support only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-LR, \-\-long-report
Generate the detailed report format.
.TP
.B \-NRT, \-\-near-real-time
Enable near-real-time supplemental signal pass.
.TP
.B \-O, \-\-output
Write report output to a file.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output machine-readable JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-explain-score
Print weighted score contribution details.
.TP
.B \-\-residence-country
Country of residence input value.
.TP
.B \-\-clearance-level
Security clearance level input value.
.TP
.B \-\-agency
Agency/department input value.
.TP
.B \-\-destination-country
Destination country input value.
.TP
.B \-\-destination-city
Destination city input value (optional).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B riskbase
returns 0 on success and non-zero if execution fails.
.SH SAFETY NOTICE
RiskBase is decision-support tooling and must not be treated as sole authority for movement decisions.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Quick posture:
.B riskbase
.TP
Long report to file:
.B riskbase -LR -O albania.txt
.TP
NRT enhanced JSON output:
.B riskbase -NRT --json
